WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.211 --> 00:00:02.291
- [Narrator] Clowns.

00:00:02.291 --> 00:00:03.531
Some love them.

00:00:03.531 --> 00:00:04.864
Lots hate them.

00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:08.989
But in the UK, it's a serious business.

00:00:08.989 --> 00:00:11.389
(charming accordion music)

00:00:11.389 --> 00:00:12.659
- Oh, sorry, just sneezed my nose off.

00:00:12.659 --> 00:00:13.492
- Oh, no.

00:00:14.381 --> 00:00:15.344
(energetic music)

00:00:15.344 --> 00:00:17.080
- [Woman Voiceover] It's a responsibility.

00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:19.741
It's for fun as well to do, of course.

00:00:19.741 --> 00:00:20.901
- [Narrator] That's Debbie.

00:00:20.901 --> 00:00:24.741
- My name's Debbie, and
I'm the Clown Egg Artist.

00:00:24.741 --> 00:00:27.421
- [Narrator] She's in charge
of the Clown Egg Registry,

00:00:27.421 --> 00:00:29.701
a collection of every single clown's face

00:00:29.701 --> 00:00:31.840
in all of the United Kingdom.

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:35.010
- Tradition of the painting
of the eggs was started

00:00:35.010 --> 00:00:38.101
first of all as a hobby by Stan Bolt.

00:00:38.101 --> 00:00:42.680
It then became a way of
recording and copyrighting

00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:46.581
the clown's face, because every
clown's face is different.

00:00:46.581 --> 00:00:50.341
Various different artists
then became the Egg Artist,

00:00:50.341 --> 00:00:53.640
and I took over six years ago.

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:55.789
- [Narrator] Debbie's job
is to paint onto an egg

00:00:55.789 --> 00:00:58.440
the unique makeup of each clown.

00:00:58.440 --> 00:01:00.611
- It's nice to have a physical object

00:01:00.611 --> 00:01:03.101
that looks like that character.

00:01:03.101 --> 00:01:05.891
It's so totally different
to having a photograph.

00:01:05.891 --> 00:01:07.960
- [Narrator] The Clown Egg
Registry is a collection

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:11.240
of dozens of eggs that
serves as an official list

00:01:11.240 --> 00:01:14.621
of each individual clown's
personality and look.

00:01:14.621 --> 00:01:17.549
- When the order comes through for an egg,

00:01:17.549 --> 00:01:20.101
the clown will send his application form,

00:01:20.101 --> 00:01:23.320
along with some samples of material,

00:01:23.320 --> 00:01:26.429
and they send photographs of
themself, different angles.

00:01:26.429 --> 00:01:29.331
I start by sketching their
portrait onto the egg,

00:01:29.331 --> 00:01:31.621
and then gradually add
color with the paint.

00:01:31.621 --> 00:01:35.880
Sometimes it's actual
hair or wool that I would

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:38.149
make into hair to put on, so
it depends on the character,

00:01:38.149 --> 00:01:40.941
but they're all there to make you laugh.

00:01:40.941 --> 00:01:42.931
Your pose again please.

00:01:42.931 --> 00:01:45.971
It's a responsibility
because it is very important

00:01:45.971 --> 00:01:48.149
to carry on that tradition.

00:01:48.149 --> 00:01:51.649
(light orchestral music)

